      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Tiny dark spots on the stems, even if you can't see any bugs, could be a sign of a fungal issue or even mineral buildup from tap water. Sometimes, the environment itself, like poor air circulation, can encourage these spots. You can try wiping the stems gently with a cloth dipped in a very diluted neem oil solution to see if that helps clear up any surface issues. If they persist, you might need to look into improving airflow around your Monstera.",
